{"trace_version":2,"pi_version":"0.87.1","subject":{"provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5"},"scenario_id":"F20-debug-agent","mode":"force","rep":0,"turn":0,"final_text":"## Bug: `parseCount` accepts suffix input like `'3x'`\nReproduction: `node --input-type=module -e \"import {parseCount} from './parse.mjs'; console.log(parseCount('3x'))\"` in disposable workspace printed `3`\nIsolated to: `parse.mjs`: `Number.parseInt(value, 10)` parses numeric prefix and ignores suffix\nHypotheses tested: `parseInt` accepts partial strings → confirmed by `'3x'` returning `3`; missing whole-string validation → confirmed by SPEC requiring entire ASCII decimal digit string\nBoundary evidence: bad value first appears at `parseCount('3x')` API boundary; `parseInt` converts it to `3` instead of rejecting\nWait condition: not applicable\nRoot cause: confirmed; `parse.mjs:1` uses `Number.parseInt`, which permits trailing junk and non-string coercions, violating SPEC PARSE-1\nFix: proved in disposable workspace only, not applied to caller: validate `typeof value === 'string'`, match `/^[0-9]+$/`, convert with `Number(value)`, then require `Number.isSafeInteger(count)`, otherwise throw `TypeError('invalid count')`\nRegression test: added SPEC QUAL-P test in sandbox; red before fix with missing exception, green after fix\nSuite: `npm test` passed in sandbox: 2 tests, 2 pass, 0 fail\nWorkspace: disposable — `/tmp/ppw-V3YwZk` removed\nBlocked: none\nNext: build","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_qfqJn1FTsd8ls41J8uNH4Avk|fc_0a97c45ab513abb0016abceaabe07c87d294ffa8e90e720b18","name":"read","args":{"path":"SPEC.md","offset":null,"limit":null},"issueIndex":0,"started_at":"2026-09-30T10:55:35.280Z","completionIndex":0,"isError":false,"result":{"bytes":461,"sha256":"b71f114b31d2927bb853ebad3ec2121b84393d1401ab77c89a223554b51eef26"},"completed_at":"2026-09-30T10:55:39.963Z"},{"id":"call_Ue1iWNDkLhTOXEgvcdmMMrkY|fc_0a97c45ab513abb0016abceaabe09087d29868ac3905605065","name":"read","args":{"path":"symptom.